WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:00.943
- Hi, it's Rie.

00:00:00.943 --> 00:00:03.820
Today I've been challenged
to take a popular food

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.750
and "Make it Fancy."

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.210
As a reminder, if you want
to check out our merch,

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.690
go to shopmakeitfancy.com.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.180
Today's challenger is Katie.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:14.013
- Hey Rie,

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:17.040
I am so excited to be
challenging you on this episode

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:17.873
of "Make it Fancy."

00:00:17.873 --> 00:00:18.800
It's been awhile.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.760
I also have become a recent member

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.760
of a very cool adult club, Costco!

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:30.110
I want you to make a Costco
rotisserie chicken fancy.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.140
I know you're gonna do
something wild and awesome,

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.750
and it's probably gonna involve booze,

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.280
so can't wait to see it.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.060
- Costco rotisserie chicken.

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:39.900
I've never had this before.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.550
And also I've never been to Costco.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.963
Oh, it's heavy, hefty.

00:00:45.582 --> 00:00:47.490
It smells good.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:48.440
It looks great.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.420
It's nice brown color.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:51.770
- [Producer] How much
do you think this costs?

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:53.412
- 12.99.

00:00:53.412 --> 00:00:55.130
- [Producer] $4.99.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:56.170
- The whole chicken?

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:57.690
Do they have their own farm?

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:01.010
So there is not a lot of
artificial ingredients.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:03.730
This is already fancy
despite of the price.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.950
I think this is the fanciest ingredients

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.623
I've ever challenged.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:10.310
Mm, well seasoned.

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:12.960
It's tender, it's a little bit dry.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.170
It's very tasty.

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.430
Seasoning is very simple.

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:19.330
I want to make something creative upgrade,

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:21.440
not a transformation for this time.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.980
This is a great challenge and as always,

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:26.841
I'm excited to "Make it Fancy."

00:01:26.841 --> 00:01:28.780
(cheerful music)

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.190
All right, here's what I got.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:32.280
Carrots, parsley, thyme,

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.350
heavy cream, oyster
mushroom, shiitake mushroom,

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:37.790
king trumpet mushroom, onions,

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:41.010
potatoes, garlic, chives, butter,

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.890
pearl onions, and pancetta.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:48.890
From the pantry, I got
flour, red wine, and brandy.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:49.953
Double alcohol.

00:01:49.953 --> 00:01:52.097
All right, let's get started.

00:01:52.097 --> 00:01:53.317
(chicken sliding)

00:01:53.317 --> 00:01:55.066
"Make it Fancy."

00:01:55.066 --> 00:01:56.230
(waltz music)

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:59.460
We have whole chicken and I use gloves.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:00.737
- [Producer] So when these come out,

00:02:00.737 --> 00:02:02.853
you have to grab them so fast

00:02:02.853 --> 00:02:04.157
'cause so many people want them.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:06.633
And the boxes are so hot.

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.220
- So you cannot hold it.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:11.650
That kind of gives me anxiety too.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:14.100
I'm not sure if I want to fight that.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.690
So I'm going to cut up chicken.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.320
Chicken has joint and you put your knife,

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:22.540
it kind of separates by itself.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:26.183
You have to cut through joints, not bone.

00:02:27.405 --> 00:02:28.900
This is thigh and leg.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:31.230
Sharp knife is important
when you are cutting

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:32.750
'cause if it's dull,

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:35.150
you cannot do a nice clean cut,

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:37.040
especially the skin.

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:38.260
The wing.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.840
Gonna use use it for later.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.760
And breast you also kind of see the line,

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:46.450
so go kind of follow that line.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:48.030
Here's your breast.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:51.670
I think if you know chicken
anatomy, it's easier too.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:52.503
Breast.

00:02:52.503 --> 00:02:54.130
Oh, I saw the wishbone.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:59.130
I'm going to use meat and
carcass in two different ways.

00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:02.060
Adding carcass in the Instant Pot.

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:06.540
I think this is also
like Instant Pot season.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.328
One onion cut in quarter.

00:03:09.328 --> 00:03:11.910
Three sprigs of thyme.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:14.890
Adding three cups of water.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:15.913
Put the lid.

00:03:17.101 --> 00:03:19.159
It's always confusing.

00:03:19.159 --> 00:03:20.040
(Rie laughing)

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.330
It's obvious I don't have it a home.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:26.260
Use pressure cook mode
and cook for 45 minutes.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:28.190
If you don't have Instant Pot at home,

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:31.426
you can just use regular pot, bring it.

00:03:31.426 --> 00:03:33.490
(Instant Pot beeping)

00:03:33.490 --> 00:03:36.970
Bring it to a boil and
cook for 20 minutes.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:40.870
I also want to use the leftover juice.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:42.410
Save this for later.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.790
45 minutes later.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:49.170
We waited a little bit so
the steam naturally released.

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:54.090
Open this and strain
the chicken stock out.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:56.980
The rotisserie chicken already seasoned

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.330
so I think it will be great for later.

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:04.070
I have Dutch oven and I'm
heating medium-low heat.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:05.650
Cook pancetta.

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:07.000
I have six ounce.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.960
I'm going to render the fat and
you want to do low and slow.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:15.960
I was advised by a few people
I should get Costco membership

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:19.910
because diapers are great deal.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:21.560
Mainly diapers.

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:25.850
Also one of my friends told
me gas is great deal as well.

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:27.540
My family is small family.

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:31.370
I don't buy a lot of bulk things

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:35.070
and if you get 34 bathroom tissue,

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:36.370
where do you store?

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:41.180
So you want to cook pancetta
low-medium heat or low heat

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:44.180
so you can render out those fat.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:45.800
If you cook high heat,

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:50.140
you get nice caramelized
and fat doesn't render.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.230
Also when you're cooking bacon,

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:56.030
you want to start with
cold pan or a low heat.

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:59.220
It's the same reason you
want to render those fat out.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:03.380
Oh, I saw someone recently
tagged me on the Instagram.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:06.460
This person made candy corn macaron

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:08.314
and Fruit Loop cream puffs.

00:05:08.314 --> 00:05:10.070
- [Producer] Oh, they're doing everything.

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:10.903
- Just two.

00:05:10.903 --> 00:05:14.010
I think this one is easy
enough to make at home,

00:05:14.010 --> 00:05:16.490
so when you make anything
from "Make it Fancy,"

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:17.670
tell me on the Instagram.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.383
My account is @thedessertsnob.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.310
Pancetta is nice and crisped up.

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:26.390
Transfer to paper towel lined plate,

00:05:26.390 --> 00:05:30.880
add one diced onion and two carrots.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:35.050
I have mixed mushroom total eight ounces.

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:37.410
I'm just using half and I'm going

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:40.520
to use remaining mushroom for later.

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:42.480
Cook until soften.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:44.870
Raise the heat to medium-high heat

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:47.189
and saute until all the ingredients

00:05:47.189 --> 00:05:50.699
are soft and begin to caramelize.

00:05:50.699 --> 00:05:54.020
- [Producer] Rie, what is the
origin of your Instagram name?

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.300
- I like dessert and when I was looking

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.670
for dessert snob was taken,

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:01.180
so I just put the dessert snob.

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:04.100
I don't know, snob is not a great word.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:05.780
So maybe I should change it.

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:07.610
All right, it looks good so I'm going

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:12.610
to add finely chopped garlic
and cook until fragrant.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:15.940
Add in two tablespoons
of tomato paste, stir in.

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:19.090
Add in one tablespoon of flour,

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:20.880
cook one to two minutes

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:24.090
so it doesn't have a like floury flavor.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:28.170
Now I'm adding about three
tablespoon of brandy.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:33.170
Deglaze bottom of the pan
where flavor is stuck.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:35.370
Two cups of red wine.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:37.303
I'm going to just go in.

00:06:37.303 --> 00:06:40.053
(wine splashing)

00:06:40.952 --> 00:06:43.702
(wine splashing)

00:06:44.628 --> 00:06:45.461
(wine splashing)

00:06:45.461 --> 00:06:47.650
Bring this to a simmer.

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:51.800
Add in one cup of chicken
stock I made earlier.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:53.660
Bay leaf and thyme.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:57.470
Bring this to simmer
and reduce this by half

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:59.707
or about 15 to 20 minutes.

00:06:59.707 --> 00:07:01.810
Sauce, it's reduced.

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:02.950
Very nice smell.

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:05.340
I wish you guys can smell.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:08.380
Add the chicken I cut earlier.

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:11.580
I feel like the breast
is a little too big,

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:13.820
so I'm going to cut in half.

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:16.720
Put the lid on top and
cook for 20 minutes.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:19.920
I'm heating up frying
pan over medium heat.

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:22.531
Melt one tablespoon of butter

00:07:22.531 --> 00:07:26.580
and add in two tablespoon of olive oil,

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.510
and heat up until butter
is completely melted.

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:32.730
Add in eight ounces of frozen pearl onion.

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:35.262
Cook until those are caramelized.

00:07:35.262 --> 00:07:36.610
Pearl onion is caramelized

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:39.720
and I'm going to add rest of the mushroom.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:40.980
Season with salt.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:44.713
Veggies are done but we
have more things to do.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:47.960
Pour plenty of water.

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:50.380
I'm adding two cup potatoes.

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:54.010
Bring it to a boil and cook
this potato until tender.

00:07:54.010 --> 00:07:55.310
So when you're cooking potato,

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:57.620
you want to make sure to
start with cold water,

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.210
because if you start
cooking with hot water,

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:03.500
outside it's cooked but
inside it doesn't cook.

00:08:03.500 --> 00:08:07.450
Potato is cooked through and
I'm going to strain water.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:10.540
You can just strain in a sink like this,

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:14.970
but this sink is fake so I'm
using strainer on the table.

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:17.903
This is not how you do it usually.

00:08:17.903 --> 00:08:19.720
You put this in a glass bowl.

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:21.500
Set aside until I use it.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:23.880
Heating up one cup of cream

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:26.650
and 10 tablespoons of butter.

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:29.230
Reserve the chicken fat and juice

00:08:29.230 --> 00:08:31.480
from the Costco rotisserie chicken.

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:34.520
Eight cloves of smashed garlic.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:35.890
Bring this to simmer.

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:37.440
The cream is come to simmer.

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:39.270
I'm going to strain this

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:43.010
and I'm adding cream
mixture little by little

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:45.410
and smash potato.

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:46.910
Add a little more.

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:50.023
I'm going to season with salt and pepper.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:54.400
The chicken fat flavor
definitely comes through.

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:57.690
The mashed potatoes taste
good and let's move on.

00:08:57.690 --> 00:09:00.000
Since Katie is coming,

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.970
I'm going to plate for her and for myself.

00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:07.770
You want to do one white
meat and one dark meat.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:12.293
So chicken breast here, chicken leg.

00:09:12.293 --> 00:09:15.610
Add this delicious sauce.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:19.020
Add rest of the chicken in here.

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:22.010
At home you can put cooked pearl onions

00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:23.830
and mushroom in the sauce,

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.610
but I think it's so pretty so I'm going

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:28.980
to just garnish afterwards.

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:32.490
I also have pancetta and I'm going

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:35.720
to use these for big plate.

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:39.524
Sprinkle some chives on the mashed potato.

00:09:39.524 --> 00:09:40.424
Pepper.

00:09:40.424 --> 00:09:41.438
Parsley.

00:09:41.438 --> 00:09:43.382
And we are done.

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:46.215
(uplifting music)

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:54.185
Costco rotisserie chicken coq au vin.

00:09:54.185 --> 00:09:55.257
Delicious.

00:09:55.257 --> 00:09:57.470
(cheerful music)

00:09:57.470 --> 00:09:59.540
Welcome back, Katie.

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:00.564
- Hi, Rie!

00:10:00.564 --> 00:10:01.397
(Rie laughing)

00:10:01.397 --> 00:10:02.230
- Are you Katie?

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:03.407
- Yeah.

00:10:03.407 --> 00:10:04.240
(Katie laughing)

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:05.080
Are you horrified?

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.470
It's really scary.

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:07.303
- If you wanna take it off?

00:10:07.303 --> 00:10:08.786
- Yeah, I do, I do.

00:10:08.786 --> 00:10:09.859
(both laughing)

00:10:09.859 --> 00:10:11.380
- It has tail and everything.

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:12.880
- It does have a tail.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.930
- I heard you recently
got a Costco membership?

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:16.763
- Yes I did.

00:10:16.763 --> 00:10:17.870
I was very excited.

00:10:17.870 --> 00:10:19.040
- Is it worth it?

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:20.340
- It is, absolutely.

00:10:20.340 --> 00:10:22.900
I was like, I don't need
this much like toilet paper,

00:10:22.900 --> 00:10:23.733
but you do.

00:10:23.733 --> 00:10:24.920
Like, it's just one trip.

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:26.018
- For you?

00:10:26.018 --> 00:10:27.160
(both laughing)

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:29.470
- I have really enjoyed
my Costco membership.

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:31.420
You need to know exactly what
you're going in there for

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:32.530
or you're going to come out with like a,

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:36.310
like a watch, and like a patio chair set.

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:39.160
- So I made a Costco
rotisserie chicken coq au vin.

00:10:39.160 --> 00:10:41.273
- I don't do anything this fancy.

00:10:41.273 --> 00:10:42.753
I just put some on the plate.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:45.920
Mm, so much flavor.

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:48.540
- I think this is very rustic French dish.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:49.740
- But it looks fancy.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:51.433
- It has brandy and it has red wine.

00:10:51.433 --> 00:10:53.660
- Ooh, I knew you were going
to do something with booze.

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:54.720
- Double alcohol.

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:55.810
- You definitely made it fancy.

00:10:55.810 --> 00:10:56.770
- Thank you.

00:10:56.770 --> 00:10:58.110
- Is it easy to upgrade like this

00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:59.370
or did this take a little bit time?

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:00.730
- No, this is super easy.

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:02.690
So like anyone can make at home.

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:04.640
We have one more thing to do.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:05.562
- What?

00:11:05.562 --> 00:11:06.395
- Oh, oh.

00:11:06.395 --> 00:11:07.228
- You.

00:11:07.228 --> 00:11:08.776
Three, two, one.

00:11:08.776 --> 00:11:10.429
- [Both] "Make it Fancy."

00:11:10.429 --> 00:11:13.096
(both laughing)

00:11:14.084 --> 00:11:16.834
(cheerful music)

